    "methodology": "Copied from NLIHC's Colorado spreadsheet for Out of Reach 2026; state figures checked against NLIHC's Colorado PDF. The housing wage is the hourly wage a full-time worker (2,080 hours a year) needs to pay the HUD Fair Market Rent at 30% of income. Counties inside a metro FMR area carry that area's rent and housing wage (nlihc_area). renter_mean_wage is NLIHC's estimated mean renter wage; NLIHC does not publish a median. gap_2br = 2-BR housing wage minus renter_mean_wage, computed here. NLIHC applies state and county minimum wages but not city ones (Denver's is not reflected)."
